{"id":66,"attempt_id":"b25d52ae-09a7-4ac0-a9f3-4503722d6e74","title":"Solve the IVP:  dy/dx = y(1 - y),  y(0) = 0.2.\nTasks:\n1) Show the equation is se","subject":"Math","is_saved":true,"created_at":"2026-02-23T08:08:04.384281","messages":[{"id":123,"role":"user","content":"Solve the IVP:  dy/dx = y(1 - y),  y(0) = 0.2.\nTasks:\n1) Show the equation is separable.\n2) Separate variables and integrate.\n3) Solve for y(x) explicitly.\n4) Apply y(0)=0.2 to find the constant.\n5) State the final closed-form solution.\n6) Find equilibrium solutions and classify them (stable/unstable).\n7) Determine lim_{xââ} y(x).\n8) Find where the solution has its inflection point (in x).\n9) Compute the time x when y(x)=0.5.\n10) Compute the time x when y(x)=0.8.\n11) Verify y(0)=0.2 by direct substitution into your formula.\n12) Plot y(x) on x â [-5, 10].\n13) Overlay a slope field on the same window (coarse grid acceptable).\n14) Plot the phase line for y' = y(1-y) on the y-axis (direction arrows).\n15) Mark and label the points where y=0.5 and y=0.8 on the solution plot.","display_markdown":null,"rendered_content":null,"media_url":null,"structured_data":null,"created_at":"2026-02-23T08:08:04.389805","model_used":null,"tokens_used":0,"input_tokens":null,"output_tokens":null,"telemetry":null},{"id":124,"role":"assistant","content":"","display_markdown":"","rendered_content":"","media_url":null,"structured_data":{"schema_version":"v2","tier":"FREE","language":{"user_language":"English","preferred_response_language":"English","response_language":"English"},"items":[{"question_id":"q1","question_index":1,"mode":"SOLVE","problem":{"original_text":"Solve the IVP:  dy/dx = y(1 - y),  y(0) = 0.2.","normalized_text":"Solve the initial value problem dy/dx = y(1-y), y(0)=0.2","detected_tasks":["solve","plot","graph"],"extra":[]},"classification":{"grade_band":"college_intro","domain":"differential_equations","topic":"first-order separable ODE / logistic equation","difficulty":"easy"},"assumptions":["Solution considered for real x and y (domain reals).","Standard logistic solution branch with 0<y<1 for initial condition y(0)=0.2."],"steps":[{"index":1,"title":"Show equation is separable","explanation":"Rewrite dy/dx = y(1-y) as dy/[y(1-y)] = dx.","math_latex":["\\frac{dy}{dx}=y(1-y)","\\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{y(1-y)}=dx"]},{"index":2,"title":"Separate variables and integrate","explanation":"Use partial fractions and integrate both sides.","math_latex":["\\frac{1}{y(1-y)}=\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{1-y}","\\int\\left(\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{1-y}\\right)dy=\\int dx","\\Rightarrow \\ln|y|-\\ln|1-y|=x+C"]},{"index":3,"title":"Solve for y(x)","explanation":"Exponentiate and solve algebraically for y.","math_latex":["\\ln\\left(\\frac{y}{1-y}\\right)=x+C","\\frac{y}{1-y}=Ce^{x}","y=\\frac{Ce^{x}}{1+Ce^{x}}=\\frac{1}{1+C^{-1}e^{-x}}"]},{"index":4,"title":"Apply initial condition","explanation":"Use y(0)=0.2 to find C.","math_latex":["y(0)=\\frac{Ce^{0}}{1+Ce^{0}}=\\frac{C}{1+C}=0.2","\\Rightarrow \\frac{C}{1+C}=\\frac{1}{5}","\\Rightarrow C=\\frac{1}{4}"]},{"index":5,"title":"Final closed-form solution","explanation":"Substitute C=1/4 into general solution.","math_latex":["y(x)=\\frac{\\tfrac{1}{4}e^{x}}{1+\\tfrac{1}{4}e^{x}}=\\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}"]},{"index":6,"title":"Equilibria and stability","explanation":"Find y* where y'=0 and classify by f'(y)=1-2y.","math_latex":["y'=y(1-y)=0\\Rightarrow y^*=0,1","f'(y)=1-2y","f'(0)=1>0\\Rightarrow y=0 \\text{ unstable}","f'(1)=-1<0\\Rightarrow y=1 \\text{ stable}"]}],"final_answer":{"answer_text":"y(x)=1/(1+4e^{-x}). Equilibria: y=0 (unstable), y=1 (stable). Limit as xââ is 1. Inflection at x=ln4. Times: y=0.5 at x=ln4, y=0.8 at x=ln16. Verification y(0)=0.2 holds.","answer_latex":"y(x)=\\dfrac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","units":null,"values":[{"label":"closed_form","value":"1/(1+4e^{-x})","value_latex":"\\dfrac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}"},{"label":"equilibria","value":"y=0 (unstable), y=1 (stable)","value_latex":"y^*=0\\ (\\text{unstable}),\\ y^*=1\\ (\\text{stable})"},{"label":"limit_at_infty","value":"1","value_latex":"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}y(x)=1"},{"label":"inflection_x","value":"ln(4)","value_latex":"x=\\ln 4"},{"label":"time_y_0.5","value":"ln(4)","value_latex":"x=\\ln 4"},{"label":"time_y_0.8","value":"ln(16)","value_latex":"x=\\ln 16"},{"label":"verification_y0","value":"y(0)=1/(1+4)=0.2","value_latex":"y(0)=\\dfrac{1}{1+4}=\\dfrac{1}{5}=0.2"}]},"plot":{"should_visualize":true,"decision_reason":"graph_mode_forced","recipe":{"plot_intent":"custom","expressions":["y(x)=1/(1+4*exp(-x))","slope_field: dy/dx = y*(1-y) (overlay)","phase_line: y' = y(1-y) on vertical y-axis"],"symbols":["x","y"],"domain":{"x_min":-5,"x_max":10,"y_min":null,"y_max":null},"axis_labels":{"x":"x","y":"y"},"sampling":{"n_points":50},"key_points":[{"label":"y=0.5","x":"ln(4)","y":0.5},{"label":"y=0.8","x":"ln(16)","y":0.8}]}},"refusal":{"is_refusal":false,"reason":null,"safe_next_step":null},"quality":{"confidence":0.9,"common_mistakes":["Sign error in partial fractions","Incorrect constant from initial condition"]},"clarification":{"needs_clarification":false,"questions":[],"note":null}}]},"created_at":"2026-02-23T08:08:04.391427","model_used":"gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07","tokens_used":5874,"input_tokens":3139,"output_tokens":2735,"telemetry":{"request_id":"89ded1bf-e300-44c9-bf90-cb76d462d1b1","attempt_id":"b25d52ae-09a7-4ac0-a9f3-4503722d6e74","tier":"SHORT_STEPS","questions_count":1,"allow_auto_split_effective":false,"model":"gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07","provider":"openai","input_tokens":3139,"output_tokens":2735,"total_tokens":5874,"latency_ms_openai":35179,"latency_ms_total":35342,"schema_name":"solve_batch_free_v2","schema_version":"v2","model_bound":"gpt-5-mini","temperature_bound":0.0,"top_p_bound":1.0,"timeout_ms_bound":60000,"max_questions_allowed_bound":15,"prompt_binding_id":"5460b7aa-7733-4f61-bac5-456c83234baa","global_system_prompt_id":"global_system_prompt_openai_v1","developer_prompt_id":"solve_dev_short_openai_v1",